{"title":"2018 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total cost of one chocolate bar and two identical packs of gums is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28eb79e5c1f857c379adaaebd3a02a5a765ae9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />. One chocolate bar costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c78cd0de09afc053c5a7244659a936a9c59df2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> more than one pack of gum.<br />\nDetermine the price of a chocolate bar.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let one piece of gum be worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> dollars. From the problem, this means that one chocolate bar costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6bcde0e66de78dde6250138abf955e45c4ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. Since the total cost of one chocolate bar and two packs of gums is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28eb79e5c1f857c379adaaebd3a02a5a765ae9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a87251ab335804a151c8b6b009398585e2b99c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + x + 1 = 4.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd597f7481bbce9bedc020fbae2dc4bf2a8d7601.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 1 = 4.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d483811c5f4ab7f43e867ff32507a233fe87346a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x = 4.15 - 1 = 3.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b015de207f7b7a32ba9af079ce07479ecdf689d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{3.15}{3} = 1.05$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"129\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Because one chocolate bar costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6bcde0e66de78dde6250138abf955e45c4ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> dollars, it must cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d0a222ac2ba83bca459b6a11cf34814bb2033e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.05 + 1 = \\boxed{2.05}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"133\" height=\"25\" /> dollars.\n</p><p>~originally by North America Math Contest Go Go Go and modified by anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let one chocolate bar be worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> dollars. From the problem, one chocolate bar costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c78cd0de09afc053c5a7244659a936a9c59df2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> more than one pack of gum, so one pack of gum costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743faf166b01e4f40cb9b5ee5347a41d7ecd18b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> dollars.\n</p><p>Since the total cost of one chocolate bar and two packs of gum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28eb79e5c1f857c379adaaebd3a02a5a765ae9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/eca6be458ce01ade37df76a365bbcc3df5e1204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(c - 1) + c = 4.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44ba7b09bf3d3816f5c7523a6e0685617b5440db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c - 2 + c = 4.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbdd5c296a7e875d51d45d30a8720a8aa04743dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3c - 2 = 4.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411897776620174bb021709040fd47eaf382015e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3c = 2 + 4.15 = 6.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"163\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/4922d00fab0f086425355fc09736e95399f4ad3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{6.15} = \\boxed{2.05}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005231\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 95/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3656/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.807      1 2018_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    5.807      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35935:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018005231 and revision id 279271. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}